# Keep Index Files In Sync

When you add, rename, delete, or significantly restructure a chapter or guide file, update both index files before finishing.

## NvidiaKokkosPrimer.md (main TOC)

Tracks: H1 title as the linked item + H2 section headings as bullet points.

- Add a numbered list item when a chapter is added
- Update bullet points when H2 headings change
- Remove the item when a chapter is deleted
- H3 sub-sections may be mentioned parenthetically only for distinct major concepts

## DOCUMENTATION_INDEX.md (quick-reference index)

Tracks: a single-sentence description of each file's scope.

- Add an entry under `## Chapters` when a chapter is added
- Add entries under `## Guides (in test_suite/)` for new guide files
- Update description only if the chapter's subject matter changes meaningfully
- Use the linked heading format: `### [`filename`](relative/path)` for all `.md` entries

## When NOT to update

Do not update either index for minor edits: adding examples, fixing typos, rewording, or adding code snippets that don't change the chapter's scope.

## Run the linter

After editing any chapter file, run the style linter on the modified file:

```bash
python style-guide/lint_docs.py <modified-file.md>
```

Fix any violations before finishing. **`SG-1-LEN` (file length) is advisory**: a modest overage above 600 lines is acceptable if the additional content is necessary for completeness and clarity of presentation. Large regressions or length increases that could be addressed by splitting a chapter should still be resolved. See `style-guide/MAINTENANCE.md` for the full update protocol.
